    {
      "texts": [
        {
          "value": "In H2b and H2s haplotype strains (e.g. C57BL/6, C57BL/10, C57L/J, LP/J, 129 and SJL/J mice), there is a deletion of 627 bp in the promoter and the first exon, leading to a failure to express the gene. In the haplotype H2q gene, an insertion in the second exon results in a frameshift and a premature stop codon, and in the haplotype H2f gene, a base substitution creates a stop codon in the first exon, leading to defective protein translation in the strains of these haplotypes"
        }
      ],
      "commentType": "POLYMORPHISM"
    },
    {
      "texts": [
        {
          "evidences": [
            {
              "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305"
            }
          ],
          "value": "Belongs to the MHC class II family"
